- BUFF DOMAIN — MECHANICAL EVALUATION SCOPE: Identify the buff source (spell name, item name,
  or class ability name) from the player's declared action and emit a mechanical_summary
  describing the effect (e.g. "Mage Armor grants +4 armor bonus to AC for 1 hour/level").
- BUFF OWNERSHIP: This domain does NOT own weapon attacks, spell attacks, damage rolls, or other
  combat attack prompts. It only identifies persistent buff effects.
- Do NOT request any dice rolls. Set player_rolls to [].
- Do NOT generate npc_actions. Set npc_actions to [].
- Do NOT generate consequences. Set consequences to [].
- Name the source precisely — the Mechanic step will receive your mechanical_summary and use it
  to decide what buffs_add mutation to emit. There is no automatic extraction; the downstream
  model reads your summary and outputs the mutation explicitly.
